  "summary": "CikaBika is a Rust-based RAT delivered through a disk image containing a decoy PDF and a double-extension LNK that drops a Nim loader, which uses an ms-settings UAC bypass to plant a sideloaded dbghelp.dll in Microsoft Edge. The RAT registers each victim with Discord for C2, exposes an operator command set (!shell, !download, !sysinfo), and exfiltrates staged archives via ngrok. The same report also covers XMRig cryptomining on a compromised AWS Bedrock AI gateway and WebDAV/Discord-linked infrastructure from AI-assisted campaigns.",
